        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: KCPT, KCTV, Public Television 19, Inc., CBS\n- Places: Kansas City, Missouri, Kansas City, Kansas, Union Hill, Blue Valley, East 31st Street, 23rd Street and Stark Avenue\n- Products: KTBG, Check, Please!\n- People: Wendall Anschutz\n\nFacts:\n- Wendall Anschutz was born on January 21, 1938.\n- Wendall Anschutz was a television newsman for KCTV in Kansas City, Missouri from 1966 until his retirement in 2001.\n- Check, Please! began airing on KCPT in Kansas City in 2009.\n- Wendall Anschutz died on January 7, 2010.\n- KCPT is owned by Public Television 19, Inc.\n- KCPT maintains studio facilities on East 31st Street in Kansas City, Missouri's Union Hill section.\n- KCPT shares its studio facilities with sister adult album alternative radio station KTBG (90.9 FM).\n- KCPT's studios are adjacent to the transmitter tower of CBS affiliate KCTV.\n- KCPT's transmitter is located near 23rd Street and Stark Avenue in Kansas City, Missouri's Blue Valley section.\n- KCTV is virtual channel 5 and broadcasts on UHF digital channel 24.\n- KCTV is a CBS-affiliated television station licensed to Kansas City, Missouri.\n- KCTV also serves Kansas City, Kansas.",
